blocks.md:
A **histogram** counts observations into configurable buckets and also tracks the sum of all observed values. For a classic histogram the client exposes:

- `<name>_bucket{le="<upper inclusive bound>"}`, one **cumulative** counter per bucket, where `le` means less or equal;
- `<name>_sum`, the total of all observed values;
- `<name>_count`, the number of observations, identical to the `le="+Inf"` bucket.

All of those are counters. An observation only increments counters, which is why histograms are cheap to record.

blocks.code:
# bounded: 20 route templates, not 2 million URIs
http_requests_total{method="POST", path="/orders/:id", status="500"}

# unbounded: one new series per order, kept forever
http_requests_total{method="POST", path="/orders/8831274", status="500"}

# the order id belongs on a span attribute or a log field,
# where the cost is per event rather than per distinct value
